<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
  <header class="mb-6">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-950">Browser extension</h1>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-700">
      Save the current page to your bookmark server from any tab, with tag autocomplete.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="mb-6 rounded-lg border border-slate-400 bg-slate-100 p-6 shadow-sm">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-950">1. Install</h2>

    <h3 class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-700">Firefox</h3>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-700">
      The extension is not yet signed by Mozilla, so stable Firefox will refuse to install it.
      Use Firefox <strong>Developer Edition</strong>, <strong>Nightly</strong>, or <strong>ESR</strong>
      with <code>xpinstall.signatures.required</code> set to <code>false</code> in
      <code>about:config</code>, then visit
      <a class="font-medium text-sky-700 hover:text-sky-900" href={~p"/extension/bookmark-server.xpi"}>
        bookmark-server.xpi
      </a>
      and accept the install prompt.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
      For a one-off without changing browser settings: open <code>about:debugging</code>
      → <em>This Firefox</em> → <em>Load Temporary Add-on…</em> and pick
      <code>manifest.json</code> from the unpacked
      <a class="font-medium text-sky-700 hover:text-sky-900" href={~p"/extension/bookmark-server.zip"}>
        zip
      </a>.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-700">Chrome / Edge</h3>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-700">
      Download
      <a class="font-medium text-sky-700 hover:text-sky-900" href={~p"/extension/bookmark-server.zip"}>
        bookmark-server.zip
      </a>
      and unzip it. Visit <code>chrome://extensions</code>, enable <em>Developer mode</em>
      (top-right), click <em>Load unpacked</em>, and select the unzipped folder.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-6 rounded-lg border border-slate-400 bg-slate-100 p-6 shadow-sm">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-950">2. Connect</h2>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-700">
      Open the extension's options page (right-click the toolbar icon → <em>Manage extension</em>
      → <em>Preferences</em>) and paste the values below. The token belongs to your account
      and lets the extension save bookmarks as you.
    </p>

    <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-[10rem_1fr]">
      <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-700">Server URL</dt>
      <dd class="min-w-0">
        <code class="block break-all rounded-md bg-white px-3 py-2 text-sm text-slate-950 border border-slate-300">
          <%= @server_url %>
        </code>
      </dd>

      <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-700">API token</dt>
      <dd class="min-w-0">
        <code class="block break-all rounded-md bg-white px-3 py-2 text-xs text-slate-950 border border-slate-300">
          <%= @token %>
        </code>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-500">
          Treat the token like a password. Reload this page to mint a fresh one;
          previous tokens stay valid until you sign out of the corresponding session.
        </p>
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="rounded-lg border border-slate-400 bg-slate-100 p-6 shadow-sm">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-950">3. Use it</h2>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-6 text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-1">
      <li>Right-click any page → <em>Save to Bookmark Server</em>.</li>
      <li>Click the toolbar icon to add or edit tags before saving.</li>
      <li>Opening the popup on an already-saved page switches into "update" mode.</li>
      <li>The options page also has a bulk-import field for a browser-exported bookmarks HTML.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</section>
